Allows butchering zombies for bones, meat and fat.

[h1] Actual features: [/h1]

[b] Butcher zombies for usefull resources: meat, bones, fat. [/b]

  Butchering zombies drains your stamina and raises your stress level.
  No way you can heartlessly tear a human flesh without feeling stressed out and exhausted.

  The income you get from butchering corpses depends on your Cooking and Short blade skills. Each level increases the chance of obtaining materials by 2 percent. From one corpse you can get up to 10 items of each type.

[h1] Right now you can use: [/h1]

  [b]Human meat ...[/b]
 [i] ... to poison someone by using it in food recipes [/i]
 [i] ... for farming as rotten food placed into composter [/i]
 [i] ... to eat it and afterall finish story of your death [/i]

 [b] Rotten bones ...[/b]
 [i] ... to make glue by performing multilevel almost realistic recipe. [/i]
     [spoiler] Shortly: you must clean the bones, crush it into dust, mix it with water and boil.[/spoiler]

  [b]Fat ...[/b]
 [i] ... to make soap by performing multilevel almost realistic recipe as well.[/i]
    [spoiler]  Shortly: you must mix soda and fat with water and boil it.[/spoiler]
 [i] ... to make candles by performing multilevel almost realistic recipe as well. [/i]
    [spoiler]  Shortly: you must boil fat and use muffin tray as mold for candles. Just wait it to cool (must be unfresh) and then extract your new candles from tray. [/spoiler]

